ution Code\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom sys import stdin\n\ndef main():\n    input = stdin.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    T = int(input[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    for _ in range(T):\n        N = int(input[idx])\n        K = int(input[idx+1])\n        idx += 2\n        \n        # Precompute allowed transitions\n        allowed = [[False] * (N + 1) for _ in range(N + 1)]\n        for a in range(1, N + 1):\n            for b in range(1, N + 1):\n                allowed[a][b] = abs(3 * a - 2 * b) <= K\n        \n        max_mask = (1 << N) - 1\n        dp = [[0] * (N + 1) for _ in range(1 << N)]\n        \n        # Initialize with single element permutations\n        for i in range(1, N + 1):\n            mask = 1 << (i - 1)\n            dp[mask][i] = 1\n        \n        # Process each mask by the number of bits set (current permutation length)\n        for m in range(1, N):  # m is the current permutation length being processed\n            for mask in range(1 << N):\n                if bin(mask).count('1') != m:\n                    continue\n                for last in range(1, N + 1):\n                    if not (mask & (1 << (last - 1))):\n                        continue\n                    if dp[mask][last] == 0:\n                        continue\n                    # Try all possible next numbers\n                    for next_num in range(1, N + 1):\n                        if mask & (1 << (next_num - 1)):\n                            continue\n                        if allowed[last][next_num]:\n                            new_mask = mask | (1 << (next_num - 1))\n                            dp[new_mask][next_num] += dp[mask][last]\n        \n        full_mask = (1 << N) - 1\n        total = sum(dp[full_mask][i] for i in range(1, N + 1))\n        print(total)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n### Explanation\n- **Dynamic Programming Table**: The DP table `dp[mask][last]` keeps track of the number of valid permutations ending with `last` us