 and others are left-associative.\n\n### Solution Code\n```python\ndef infix_to_rpn(expr):\n    precedence = {'^': 4, '*': 3, '/': 3, '+': 2, '-': 2}\n    output = []\n    stack = []\n    for char in expr:\n        if char.isalpha():\n            output.append(char)\n        elif char == '(':\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char == ')':\n            while stack and stack[-1] != '(':\n                output.append(stack.pop())\n            stack.pop()  # Remove '(' from the stack\n        else:\n            # Handle operators\n            while stack and stack[-1] != '(' and (\n                (precedence.get(stack[-1], 0) > precedence.get(char, 0)) or\n                (precedence.get(stack[-1], 0) == precedence.get(char, 0) and char != '^')\n            ):\n                output.append(stack.pop())\n            stack.append(char)\n    # Pop any remaining operators from the stack to the output\n    while stack:\n        output.append(stack.pop())\n    return ''.join(output)\n\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    n = int(sys.stdin.readline())\n    for _ in range(n):\n        expr = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n        print(infix_to_rpn(expr))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n### Explanation\n1. **Reading Input**: The code reads the number of test cases and each subsequent algebraic expression.\n2. **Processing Each Expression**: For each character in the expression:\n   - **Operands** (letters) are directly added to the output list.\n   - **Left Parentheses** are pushed onto the stack.\n   - **Right Parentheses** trigger popping from the stack to the output until a left parenthesis is encountered.\n   - **Operators** are managed based on their precedence and associativity. Higher or equal precedence operators (considering associativity) are popped from the stack to the output before the current operator is pushed onto the stack.\n3. **Finalizing Output**: After processing all characters, any remaining operators in the stack are popped to