irst, determine the positions of all set bits in the binary representation of N. These positions will help us generate all possible subsets of these bits.\n2. **Generate Subsets**: Using the positions of set bits, generate all possible combinations (subsets) of these bits. Each combination can be represented using a bitmask where each bit in the mask indicates whether a corresponding bit position in N is included in the subset.\n3. **Compute Values**: For each subset (represented by a bitmask), compute the corresponding integer value by summing the powers of 2 for each included bit position.\n4. **Sort and Return**: Sort the generated values in descending order and return them.\n\n### Solution Code\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def printSubsets(self, N):\n        positions = []\n        current_bit = 0\n        temp = N\n        while temp > 0:\n            if temp & 1:\n                positions.append(current_bit)\n            temp >>= 1\n            current_bit += 1\n        \n        m = len(positions)\n        res = []\n        for mask in range(1 << m):\n            current = 0\n            for j in range(m):\n                if mask & (1 << j):\n                    current += 1 << positions[j]\n            res.append(current)\n        \n        res.sort(reverse=True)\n        return res\n```\n\n### Explanation\n1. **Identify Set Bits**: The loop iterates through each bit of N, collecting the positions of all set bits. For example, if N is 5 (binary 101), the positions collected are [0, 2].\n2. **Generate Subsets**: Using bitmasking, we generate all possible subsets of the collected positions. Each bitmask from 0 to 2^m - 1 (where m is the number of set bits) represents a different subset. For each bitmask, we check which bits are set and include the corresponding positions from the list of set bits.\n3. **Compute Values**: For each subset, the value is computed by summing 2 raised to the power of each included position. This converts the subset of bit posi